  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## Rescan with the L=1-derived reference factors: **49/49 pass**\n\nThe L=1 derivation (`SU3_L1_GeneralRep_Normalization.wb`) matches direct diagonalization at finite twist. It moves the reference SoV points with $\\lambda_2$ of the site. Per site $s$:\n$$\n\\Psi^{\\rm ref}=\\prod_s Q_1(\\theta_s+\\lambda^{(s)}_2)\\big[Q_1(\\theta_s)Q_2(\\theta_s-1)-Q_2(\\theta_s)Q_1(\\theta_s-1)\\big],\\qquad\nc^{\\rm ref}=\\prod_s Q^3(\\theta_s)\\big[Q^3(\\theta_s)Q^2(\\theta_s+\\lambda^{(s)}_2+1)-Q^2(\\theta_s)Q^3(\\theta_s+\\lambda^{(s)}_2+1)\\big].\n$$\nEverything else is unchanged: ladder poles, $c=(\\lambda^{(1)}_1-\\lambda^{(1)}_3)+(\\lambda^{(2)}_1-\\lambda^{(2)}_3)+1$, $E_\\lambda$, $\\mathcal N$. The physical limits are the ones from section 3; only the untwisted side was rebuilt.\n\n- **All 49 ordered pairs pass**, 121 non-vacuum hw states in total. Worst $|{\\rm rhs}/{\\rm lhs}-1|=8.7\\times10^{-17}$, which is the $\\varepsilon$-extrapolation error.\n- **$c\\pm1$ fails for every pair.** The weakest contrast is $3.9\\%$ (pairs $[1,0,0]\\otimes[2,2,0]$, $[1,1,0]\\otimes[3,0,0]$, $[1,1,0]\\otimes[3,1,0]$ and their swaps); all others are above $10\\%$.\n- $c^{\\rm ref}\\Psi^{\\rm ref}\\neq0$ for every state, so the $[2,2,0]$ pairs are now defined.\n- **Single-term $c^{\\rm ref}$ suffices.** The old adjoint form $\\tfrac14[D(1;0,0)-D(0;0,1)]$ only adds a term that does not change the ratios for $\\lambda_2=1$.\n- **Scope.** One chain point $\\theta=(1/3,-8/57)$, two twist directions, all reps with $\\lambda_3=0$. The $\\lambda_3$ dependence and $E_\\lambda$ are still identified, not derived.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- 5. Why c^ref is one term. The old adjoint form was (D(1;0,0) - D(0;0,1))/4, with\n   D(1;0,0) = q^3(th+1) W(th),  W(x) = q^3(x) q^2(x+1) - q^2(x) q^3(x+1)  (dual Casoratian).\n   Check on the untwisted hw states whether W(th_s + k) = 0 for k = 0..l2^(s), per site, for every pair.\n   Entries: \"0\" = vanishes to the 60-digit working precision for every hw state; otherwise the largest relative size. ---- *)\nClearAll[casTabS, casRowS, casLogS];\ncasRowS[r1_, r2_] := Module[{lam2 = {r1[[2]], r2[[2]]}},\n   setupChainS[r1, r2];\n   hwOpS = Normal[Join[EtotS[1, 2], EtotS[2, 3]]];\n   untwS = buildUntwS[];\n   Table[With[{qd = Function[{j, x}, qpolyS[N[s[\"qd\"][[j]], 60], x]]},\n      Table[With[{th = thetaS[[site]]},\n        Table[Abs[qd[3, th + k] qd[2, th + k + 1] - qd[2, th + k] qd[3, th + k + 1]]/\n           (Abs[qd[3, th + k] qd[2, th + k + 1]] + Abs[qd[2, th + k] qd[3, th + k + 1]]), {k, 0, lam2[[site]]}]], {site, 2}]],\n     {s, untwS}]];\ncasTabS = Table[With[{t = casRowS[r1, r2]},\n    {Row[r1, \",\"], Row[r2, \",\"],\n     Row[Table[Row[{\"site \", site, \": \", Row[Table[With[{m = Max[t[[All, site, k + 1]]]}, If[m == 0, \"0\", ScientificForm[N[m, 2]]]],\n           {k, 0, {r1, r2}[[site, 2]]}], \"  \"]}], {site, 2}], \"     \"]}],\n   {r1, repsS}, {r2, repsS}];\n(* Summary: W vanishes at th_s + k exactly for k < l2^(s), and not at k = l2^(s). *)\ncasLogS = And @@ Flatten@Table[With[{t = casRowS[r1, r2]},\n     Table[(Max[t[[All, site, k + 1]]] == 0) === (k < {r1, r2}[[site, 2]]), {site, 2}, {k, 0, {r1, r2}[[site, 2]]}]], {r1, repsS}, {r2, repsS}];\nColumn[{\n  Grid[{{\"all 49 pairs, both sites: W(theta_s + k) = 0 exactly for k < lambda2^(s), nonzero at k = lambda2^(s)\", casLogS}},\n   Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left],\n  Grid[Prepend[Flatten[casTabS, 1], {\"site 1\", \"site 2\", \"max over hw states of |W(theta_s + k)|/scale, k = 0..lambda2^(s)\"}],\n   Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]}]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
