   "value": "(* ---- 6b. The [2,2,2] and [1,1,1] pairs above have a single hw state (the vacuum), so they test nothing.\n   Two non-trivial replacements, including new content ([4,4,1] ~ [3,3,0], [3,2,1] x [5,3,2] ~ adjoint x [3,1,0] shifted by 2). ---- *)\nClear[NotebookSource];\nClearAll[lam3ExtraS];\nlam3ExtraS = Table[With[{old = runPairS @@ pr},\n    Module[{gen = rescanWithS[old, BgenS], deg = degGenOKS @@ pr, ns = rescanWithS[old, BnewS]},\n     <|\"pair\" -> pr, \"checks\" -> (old[\"qdetOK\"] && old[\"nTwOK\"] && deg), \"kappa\" -> old[\"kappa\"], \"c\" -> old[\"c\"],\n      \"gen\" -> gen, \"noShift\" -> ns|>]], {pr, {{{3, 2, 1}, {4, 4, 1}}, {{2, 2, 1}, {5, 3, 2}}}}];\nGrid[Prepend[lam3RowS /@ lam3ExtraS, {\"site 1\", \"site 2\", \"# hw\", \"checks (qdet, degrees, twisted match)\", \"c (rule)\", \"c derived\",\n    \"max |rhs/lhs - 1|, lambda3-shifted\", \"c+-1 contrast\", \"control: without lambda3 shifts\", \"\"}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
