  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## $\\lambda_3\\neq0$ (sections 6, 6b)\n\nA site in $\\lambda'+(k,k,k)$ is the $\\lambda'$ site at $\\theta+k$. The general reference wave functions are therefore\n$$\n\\Psi_{\\mu,0}=\\prod_s q_1(\\theta_s+\\lambda^{(s)}_2)\\big[q_1(\\theta_s+\\lambda^{(s)}_3)q_2(\\theta_s+\\lambda^{(s)}_3-1)-q_2(\\theta_s+\\lambda^{(s)}_3)q_1(\\theta_s+\\lambda^{(s)}_3-1)\\big],\n$$\n$$\n\\bar\\Psi_{\\mu,0}=\\prod_s q^3(\\theta_s+\\lambda^{(s)}_3)\\big[q^3(\\theta_s+\\lambda^{(s)}_3)q^2(\\theta_s+\\lambda^{(s)}_2+1)-q^2(\\theta_s+\\lambda^{(s)}_3)q^3(\\theta_s+\\lambda^{(s)}_2+1)\\big],\n$$\nwith untwisted degrees $\\deg q_i=(D-\\mu_i)+(i-1)$ and $\\deg q^j=\\mu_j-\\Lambda_3+(3-j)$, where $\\Lambda_3=\\lambda^{(1)}_3+\\lambda^{(2)}_3$.\n\n**Full pipeline, including the twisted limit.** The formula passes on the 8 pairs with more than one hw state:\n- the pairs: $[2,1,1]\\otimes[2,1,0]$, $[3,2,1]\\otimes[3,1,0]$, $[2,1,0]\\otimes[3,3,1]$, $[4,1,1]\\otimes[1,1,0]$, $[3,2,1]^{\\otimes2}$, $[2,1,1]\\otimes[4,3,1]$, $[3,2,1]\\otimes[4,4,1]$, $[2,2,1]\\otimes[5,3,2]$;\n- residuals $10^{-19}$–$10^{-20}$;\n- $c\\pm1$ contrast $\\ge7\\%$;\n- $c$ from $\\Delta T_2$ equals the rule in every case;\n- control without the $\\lambda_3$ shifts fails at $O(1)$.\n\nThe $[2,2,2]$ and $[1,1,1]$ pairs have only the vacuum, so they are vacuous.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- 7. QQ structure of the reference brackets (exact). Conjecture, per site ladder factors F:\n   W12(u) = q_1(u) q_2(u-1) - q_2(u) q_1(u-1) = K12 q^3(u) prod_s prod_{k = l2^(s)+1}^{l1^(s)} (u - th_s - k),\n   W(u)   = q^3(u) q^2(u+1) - q^2(u) q^3(u+1) = K  q_1(u) prod_s prod_{k = l3^(s)}^{l2^(s)-1} (u - th_s - k).\n   Test: the ratios are u-independent constants (exact, RootReduce), for every hw state of several pairs.\n   (The first numerical shift search in this cell was unreliable and has been replaced.) ---- *)\nClearAll[qqPolyS, divShiftS, rootLabelS, qqTabS, qqPairsS, rootsOfS, qqDataS, qqCheckS, ladderS];\nladderS[x_, from_Integer, to_Integer, th_] := Product[x - th - k, {k, from, to}];\nqqCheckS[pr_] := (setupChainS @@ pr; hwOpS = Normal[Join[EtotS[1, 2], EtotS[2, 3]]]; untwS = buildUntwS[];\n   Table[Module[{x, q1, q2, qd2, qd3, W12, W, F12, F, r12, r},\n     q1 = qpolyS[s[\"q\"][[1]], x]; q2 = qpolyS[s[\"q\"][[2]], x]; qd2 = qpolyS[s[\"qd\"][[2]], x]; qd3 = qpolyS[s[\"qd\"][[3]], x];\n     W12 = q1 (q2 /. x -> x - 1) - q2 (q1 /. x -> x - 1);\n     W = qd3 (qd2 /. x -> x + 1) - qd2 (qd3 /. x -> x + 1);\n     F12 = Product[ladderS[x, {pr[[1]], pr[[2]]}[[t, 2]] + 1, {pr[[1]], pr[[2]]}[[t, 1]], thetaS[[t]]], {t, 2}];\n     F = Product[ladderS[x, {pr[[1]], pr[[2]]}[[t, 3]], {pr[[1]], pr[[2]]}[[t, 2]] - 1, thetaS[[t]]], {t, 2}];\n     r12 = RootReduce[Together[W12/(qd3 F12)]]; r = RootReduce[Together[W/(q1 F)]];\n     {Row[pr[[1]], \",\"], Row[pr[[2]], \",\"], Row[s[\"mu\"], \",\"], FreeQ[r12, x] && r12 =!= 0, FreeQ[r, x] && r =!= 0}], {s, untwS}]);\nqqPairsS = {{{3, 1, 0}, {2, 2, 0}}, {{4, 1, 1}, {2, 0, 0}}, {{2, 1, 0}, {3, 1, 0}}, {{3, 0, 0}, {3, 3, 1}}, {{2, 2, 1}, {5, 3, 2}}, {{3, 1, 0}, {3, 1, 0}}};\nqqTabS = Flatten[qqCheckS /@ qqPairsS, 1];\nColumn[{\n  Grid[{{\"all hw states of all pairs: both factorizations hold exactly\", And @@ Flatten[qqTabS[[All, 4 ;; 5]]]}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left],\n  Grid[Prepend[qqTabS, {\"site 1\", \"site 2\", \"mu\", \"W12 = K q^3(u) prod_s prod_{k=l2+1}^{l1}(u-th_s-k)\", \"W = K q_1(u) prod_s prod_{k=l3}^{l2-1}(u-th_s-k)\"}],\n   Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]}]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
