   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- 9. Symmetry question. The simplified normalization carries R = prod_s q^3(th_s+l2)/q^3(th_s+l3) on top of the symmetric\n   1/prod_s (q_1(th_s+l2) q^3(th_s+l3))^2. Is R state-independent (so it could be dropped), or even a function of mu only?\n   Also test the symmetric alternative directly: B_sym = det N/((mu1-mu3+1)!(mu1-mu2+1)!(mu2-mu3+1)! prod_s q_1(th_s+l2)^2 q^3(th_s+l3)^2)\n   against the physical limits of section 3. ---- *)\nClearAll[ratioRS, symTabS, BsymS];\nratioRS[m_] := Product[With[{th = thetaS[[s]], a = {rep1S, rep2S}[[s, 2]], b = {rep1S, rep2S}[[s, 3]]},\n    qpolyS[N[untwS[[m, \"qd\"]][[3]], 250], th + a]/qpolyS[N[untwS[[m, \"qd\"]][[3]], 250], th + b]], {s, 2}];\nBsymS[m_, c_] := Module[{q, qd, Nm, mu = untwS[[m, \"mu\"]], den},\n   q = Function[{i, x}, qpolyS[N[untwS[[m, \"q\"]][[i]], 250], x]];\n   qd = Function[{j, x}, qpolyS[N[untwS[[m, \"qd\"]][[j]], 250], x]];\n   Nm = Table[{\n      bracketS[Function[x, qd[ij[[2]], x + 1] q[ij[[1]], x] - qd[ij[[2]], x] q[ij[[1]], x]]],\n      bracketS[Function[x, x qd[ij[[2]], x] q[ij[[1]], x - 1] - (x - c) qd[ij[[2]], x + 1] q[ij[[1]], x]]],\n      bracketS[Function[x, qd[ij[[2]], x] q[ij[[1]], x - 1] - qd[ij[[2]], x + 1] q[ij[[1]], x]]]}, {ij, {{1, 3}, {1, 2}, {2, 3}}}];\n   den = (mu[[1]] - mu[[3]] + 1)! (mu[[1]] - mu[[2]] + 1)! (mu[[2]] - mu[[3]] + 1)! Product[With[{th = thetaS[[s]], a = {rep1S, rep2S}[[s, 2]], b = {rep1S, rep2S}[[s, 3]]},\n       q[1, th + a]^2 qd[3, th + b]^2], {s, 2}];\n   Det[Nm]/den];\nsymTabS = Table[With[{old = runPairS @@ pr},\n    setupChainS @@ pr; hwOpS = Normal[Join[EtotS[1, 2], EtotS[2, 3]]]; untwS = buildUntwS[]; setPolesS[];\n    With[{R = Table[ratioRS[m], {m, Length[untwS]}], bs = Table[BsymS[m, cRuleS @@ pr], {m, Length[untwS]}],\n      lhs = old[\"states\"][[All, \"lhs\"]]},\n     {Row[pr[[1]], \",\"], Row[pr[[2]], \",\"], Length[untwS], Column[N[R/R[[1]], 8]],\n      N[Max[Abs[(bs/bs[[1]])/lhs - 1][[2 ;;]]], 3]}]], {pr, {{{2, 1, 0}, {2, 1, 0}}, {{3, 1, 0}, {2, 2, 0}}, {{2, 1, 1}, {4, 3, 1}}, {{1, 1, 0}, {1, 0, 0}}}}];\nGrid[Prepend[symTabS, {\"site 1\", \"site 2\", \"# hw\", \"R/R_vac per hw state\", \"symmetric B_sym: max |rhs/lhs - 1|\"}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
